{
  "info": {
    "name": "Monster Raid (Lab 2)",
    "description": "tamagotchi-monster-raid-service:0.3.0 behind the gateway (base_url = gateway, http://localhost:8080; the service port is not published). The first request logs Alice, Bob and a freshly registered outsider in through User Management (POST /api/v1/auth/login, seed password password123) and sends their access tokens as Authorization: Bearer; the gateway turns them into X-Auth-User-Id / X-Auth-Roles. Internal routes send the service credential in service_token (set it in the environment). There is no RabbitMQ, so the first request creates a raid through the temporary POST /internal/v1/dev/raid-events; each run uses a new schedule_id. Real data through the gateway: guild Founders (Alice, Bob, Carol) from Guild, raid definition Big Slime v1 (300 HP) and care definitions from Package Registry, Alice's primary pet (read from GET /api/v1/tamagotchi-selections/me) reserved and settled by Tamagotchi. The run attacks until the monster dies, so the settlement frees the pet again and the collection can be re-run. The last folder checks the live HP stream (SSE) on a raid that has already ended, so the stream closes on its own.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "broker_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8090",
